      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transport From Bangalore To Bajagoli</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p><ul>
   <p>Following the visual assessment, the agent must perform an accurate odometer verification against the LR bilty. The LR bilty serves as the official transport document recording the vehicle’s mileage at the point of origin. The delivery personnel should note the exact odometer reading displayed on the motorcycle’s dashboard and cross-reference it with the documented figure. Discrepancies exceeding the permitted tolerance threshold must be flagged, investigated, and formally noted on the delivery manifest. This verification prevents unauthorized usage during transit and establishes a clear accountability trail for both the carrier and the consignee.</p>
   <p>Once visual and mileage checks are complete, the process concludes with a signed condition sign-off. The receiving party must review all documented findings, acknowledge the vehicle’s current status, and affix their signature to the electronic or physical delivery receipt. Simultaneously, the delivery agent countersigns to confirm procedural compliance.</p>
<p>Both parties should retain copies of the signed document, along with timestamped verification photographs, for audit and dispute resolution purposes. This structured handover methodology minimizes liability, ensures transparent communication, and guarantees that every two-wheeler reaches its destination in the exact condition documented at departure.</p></div>
